WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:05.900
The scenery and buildings of the town have changed much in the last five years.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.890
During that time, I, and the people around me, have changed as well.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.860
It's not something that we can do anything about.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.450
Not everything that has changed is bad though.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.700
But, there are things that I wish had never changed.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.280
There are things that I wished stayed the way they were forever...

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.260
...like the things inside the memories of my childhood.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.050
Yuzuki-sensei.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.520
We've brought the homework exercise books.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.180
Ah, good work.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.010
Please leave them here.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.380
Thanks.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.860
How is it? Have you gotten used to the school yet?

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.410
Yes, in class, there's Shuu and Nana...

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:00.970
I mean, Yatsushiro-san and others who are my childhood friends.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.380
I see, that's good.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.410
Then, we'll be going now.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.030
Wait a sec.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.960
Hold out your hands please.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.900
Here.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.600
Here.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.650
Keep this a secret from the others, okay?

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.190
Sure.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.560
Excuse us.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:52.170
That's right, this is the first time you've received teacher's caramel.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:57.850
Once in a while, Yuzuki-sensei would give caramels as a reward.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:03.140
All the other students know about it already, so it's kinda late to keep it a secret.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.370
I see.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.750
<b>Teacher's Caramel</b>

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:20.380
You're organising a petition to oppose what?

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:28.120
It seems like there's a plan to level the Sakuranomori nature park to erect a new town hall.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.140
What? They're going to level the nature park?

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.850
Yeah, it's ridiculous, isn't it?

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:38.140
It's always been a place of relaxation that everyone loves.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:41.290
Moreover, there are rare plants and such there too.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:48.160
Honestly, they should be thinking about conservation. It's a place that everyone should treasure.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:52.310
If it's such an important place, why are they planning to level it then?

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.290
To put it simply, it's the scheming of businessmen.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:57.850
Scheming.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.110
It seems like they're planning to build a ridiculously luxurious town hall.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:07.040
They definitely paid a large sum in bribes to get hold of the construction permit.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.460
That's horrible!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.560
Right?

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.500
I went on a school trip there during elementary school...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.470
...and I went hiking there with my family on Sundays as well.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.140
Yeah, I've been there.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.230
Me too.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:22.940
I've been there too.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:29.590
I remember when we were kids, my mum would take me and Shuusuke there.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.110
That sure brings back memories.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:51.200
I don't know why, but I sense you're reminiscing about something quite unpleasant.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:57.170
So there you have it.
 I'd like everyone to help by signing this petition.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.390
Sure, I'll sign the petition!

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:04.150
I don't want the nature park to disappear either.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:08.440
Afterwards, I'll talk to my class and have them sign it as well.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:12.290
As expected from a final year student. You're really dependable!

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:16.230
I'll try talking to the guys at the Kendo club.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.150
Please do. I'm counting on you.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.040
To start off, let me sign the petition then.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:24.330
I've already written your name down though.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.120
Hey, you can't do that!

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.230
Why not? Twins are of one mind anyway.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:34.080
Then you wouldn't mind if I ate your pudding as well!

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.840
Don't be stupid! That's a different thing altogether!

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.330
We may be twins, but we have separate stomachs, right?!

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:43.100
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 69 0 69

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:43.100
This line is an idiom for, "There's always room for dessert."

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:44.100
<i>No, I'm not gonna say it. 
"Separate stomachs" has a different meaning.</i>

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.100
m 0 0 l 500 0 500 69 0 69

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.100
This line is an idiom for, "There's always room for dessert."

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:53.550
Have you been doing the classroom cleaning until now?

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:54.250
Yes.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.130
It sure took a while.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:59.150
Yeah, we were doing it thoroughly.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.730
I see, then well done.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.710
But probably, the boys were playing baseball by pitching a rag and swinging broomsticks, right?

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:09.950
I did things like that too when I was in school.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.580
Well, in spite of that, good work with the cleaning.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.760
Hold out your hand.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.650
Here's your reward.

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:24.850
What's the matter?

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.980
No, nothing at all.
I'll be going now.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.390
Okay, goodbye. See you again tomorrow.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.400
It's sure getting late.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:27.910
That's it!

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.310
I remember.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.650
What's wrong? Giving up already?

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.980
Here, I'm going to give you this.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:14.910
Cheer up and try again.

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:38.130
So, Yuzuki-sensei was the girl with the caramel back then.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:41.460
Hidaka-kun.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.650
What are you up to?

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:45.960
Hoshino-san?

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:53.050
Are you okay?

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.810
Next Saturday?

00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:01.410
Yeah, I'll be going to the old-folks' home with Shuri.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.080
I was wondering if you'd like to come along.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:08.450
Sure, I don't really have any plans this Sunday, so I'll go.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:10.420
Thanks. It'll be a great help.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.810
Play with Yokoi-san again, 'kay?

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.750
Yokoi-san?

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.680
Wakatsuki-san, I called you here today because of this.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:34.620
That's the...?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.830
It looks like you know what it is.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.040
Yes, but is there a problem?

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.350
Yes, there is!

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.890
This is political campaigning!

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:46.510
This isn't political campaigning!

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:49.840
I'm just requesting signatures from friends.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:55.610
That's right! It's not like she's standing in front of the school gate and calling out to people.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:59.290
She's only asking assistance from her own friends.

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:02.960
Also, what she's doing isn't against the law.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:06.030
So, I didn't think that it'd be such a big deal.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:08.210
It is a big deal.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:16.130
The plan to build a new town hall was promoted by her father, the city councillor.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.910
If you take that into consideration, there is no way we could approve this.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:23.750
Hold it right there. This is a school!

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:29.740
You're limiting a student's actions with those reasons? I think you're the ones with the bigger problem.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:36.740
What are you saying? Her father sent her here and we have to repay...

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:44.660
Wakatsuki-san, no matter the reason, you are not permitted to do something like this again.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.930
Understood?

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:55.900
Umm, what is this?

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.090
Eating to feel better.

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.750
Eating to feel better?

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:02.380
When you feel like this, how can you not eat?

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.000
Actually, I wanted to bring you drinking.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.710
But since you're underage, I can't.

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.130
C'mon, hurry and eat up.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:13.660
There are three more dishes coming, so we have to make space.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:14.980
Okay.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.950
I think we ate too much.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:28.360
Ordering sakuramochi sundae for dessert on top of all that was a bad idea.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.570
I guess that was rather thoughtless.

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:33.790
But since it was a limited time offer, I just had to.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.510
That was close.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.490
We almost had a disaster there, didn't we?

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:52.780
Hey sensei, how bout hitting up the karaoke box to help digest the food?

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:58.070
That sounds great! But, I'm warning you, I'm pretty good with songs from the 80's!

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:02.140
I won't be so easily beaten. I've got a secret weapon up my sleeve.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:05.030
All right, let's go bring the house down then!

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.830
I'm home.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:21.560
Shuri-san, your father is waiting for you in the living room.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.150
Shuri! Come here for a second!

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.670
You're back rather late.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:35.390
Where have you been all night?

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:37.310
Does it matter where I was?

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:40.460
I got a call from your school a while earlier.

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:42.830
What are you trying to do?

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:45.710
Soliciting signatures to oppose the new town hall?

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:53.060
There's no way you're unaware that I'm the central figure of the project.

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:58.140
It's because the nature park is a really precious place.

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:01.810
For Shuusuke and myself, and also mother...

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:06.280
Mother? What does Sayuka have to do with the nature park?

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:12.490
Our real mother is the one who gave birth to me and Shuusuke.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:17.390
Don't call this woman you use only for sex, my mother.

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:19.800
Shuri, that's too much!

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:24.560
Shuusuke and I have never thought of that woman as our mother. Not even once!

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:29.420
That woman who came into our house just because of money...

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:30.950
That's enough!

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.310
Wait, Shuri!

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:44.600
I'm not done talking yet. Shuri!

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:13.870
I wonder why Shuri was absent from school.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.400
Maybe she caught a cold.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:18.730
I asked Shuu, but he wouldn't say clearly.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.260
I see.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.850
Perhaps, it's that...

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.200
What do you mean?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:29.140
I mean, how do I put it? A girl's...

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.410
A girl's what?

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:36.880
If you don't understand then nevermind.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.600
Good afternoon.

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.530
Ah, welcome.

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:45.110
Oh, you've come! I've been waiting for you, young man!

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.080
Hello.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.000
Good afternoon, Yokoi-san.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:51.710
Quit standing there and let's go already!

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:55.740
I've been itching to play all day.

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:01.510
He seems to have taken a great liking to him.

00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:02.520
That's true.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:05.890
Yokoi-san has been feeling much better because of him.

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:09.210
If you have a purpose then you'll work harder.

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:10.570
I'm really grateful.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.300
Is something wrong?

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:20.850
I was just wondering why Poe hasn't come out to greet me today.

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:24.530
Ah, he's been missing since yesterday.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:28.030
It's okay. I'm sure he'll be back when he gets hungry.

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:31.440
That's right. He'll surely come back then.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:47.450
Young man, one more round, one more round!

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:51.130
Yokoi-san, isn't that enough?

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:53.620
Don't take the young man all for yourself.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:56.380
C'mon, the tea is ready.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.760
Let's take a short break then.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:10.950
Ah, Kaji-san.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:12.300
Hello.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.640
Pardon our intrusion.

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:15.630
Welcome.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:21.010
Where's the long-haired girl who came with you last time?

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:24.030
Well... Nanaka is kinda busy.

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:27.440
I see. What a pity.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:30.330
Why don't you join us for tea, Kaji-san?

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:34.050
No thanks, I just came to borrow a pair of scissors.

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.580
I see.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:41.440
Oh yeah, before going back, can you two come to my room?

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.800
I have a small favour to ask.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:44.680
Sure.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:45.810
Sure thing.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:52.070
Okay, young man. You've had plenty of rest right? Let's go for another round!

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.040
What? Still more?

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:56.050
Come now, don't complain.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.150
Because, when one is popular, they are like flowers.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:15:59.380
Hey, look here!

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:04.890
You can do that?

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.210
Damnit.

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:12.980
That's right. Next, you do it like this over there.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:14.950
You're really good.

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:20.120
Come in.

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:26.880
Forgive me for asking you to come to my room.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.780
No, not at all.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:31.840
So, what was the favour you wanted?

00:16:35.690 --> 00:16:38.390
That box on the bed.

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:43.040
I'd like to bury that under a sakura tree on the elder sister hill.

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:44.150
This?

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.490
Yes.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:50.130
If possible, please bury it under a big tree.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:52.490
Okay, that's fine.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.660
Thank you. It's a great help.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:56.780
Not at all.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:59.160
But, what's inside?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.730
That's a secret.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:06.800
But, it's something really nice.

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:14.500
We'll be going now.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.030
Please come again.

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:16.990
Sure.

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:20.230
You can return the shovel then.

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:21.010
Okay.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.560
Young man, I'm going to improve my skills before you come next time.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.050
Look forward to it!

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:27.110
Okay...

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:29.940
Goodbye. Take care.

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.260
Goodbye.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.150
They're liking you more each time.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.660
Hey, wasn't that sound the bell from Poe's collar?

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.370
Poe's?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.730
There, again.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.440
I can't hear it though.

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:50.240
I'm certain I heard it.

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:54.920
Poe! Where are you? Stop hiding and come out.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.150
Poe!

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:11.200
Kaji-san wanted it buried under the largest tree possible, but how are we going to find it?

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:13.160
That's why we came here.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:17.010
The largest tree on the elder sister hill...

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:19.730
...would probably be that one?

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.950
Which?

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.440
I'm going now.

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:36.340
Let's see, konnyaku jelly, cucumbers, carrots, and then...

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:46.850
How did you know there was a large tree here?

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:50.180
We used to run around a lot here everyday when we were kids.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:55.860
So, I remember where the large trees, strange stones, and such were.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.260
Ah, that's why.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:19:03.520
But, I'm kinda surprised that it's exactly where I pictured it in my memories.

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:09.120
But, why does she want it buried?

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:13.190
Kaji-san said that it was something like a charm.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:16.860
Should we open it and see what's inside?

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:18.440
We can't do that!

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:20.100
I guess not...

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:24.650
That should do it.

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:27.360
Then, let's bury it.

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:46.530
Are you okay?

00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:49.240
Sorry, I'm feeling a little light-headed.

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:51.250
But, I'm okay now.

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:56.850
Don't exert yourself.
You should keep still for a while.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.340
I'm sorry.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:42.440
Thank you. I'm okay now, really.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.890
Okay, then...

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:54.950
Poe, where are you?

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:58.100
Dinner time! Quit playing and come out!

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:00.730
Poe! Poe?

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:06.680
This <i>is</i> odd. Where did he go?

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:28.330
The sepia coloured memory album.

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:32.000
Inside is the unfading, all red mail box.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:36.380
The keys of memories, opening the doors to a nostalgic past...

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.090
...and the feelings with no where to go spill out.

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:43.200
Next time on Myself; Yourself: The Secret Mail Box.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:45.580
I give to you, these feelings inside my heart.

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:49.150
That sounds kinda conceited, doesn't it?

